# 5. Dashboard Requirements

## 5.1 Dashboard Title

Dashboard title:

**Exceed Lanka Prosthetic & Orthotic Data Management System**

## 5.2 Main Dashboard Cards

The dashboard must show the following main cards.

### 5.2.1 Total Patients

Shows the total number of registered patients.

Users should be able to drill down and view the patient list behind the count.

### 5.2.2 Active Records

Recommended meaning:

**Active Records should mean active patient treatment records / active patient episodes.**

This is the best option because one patient can have more than one prosthetic or orthotic case over time.

So the dashboard should use:

* Label: **Active Records**
* Meaning: active treatment records or active episodes under patients

Each active record belongs to a patient number.

Users should be able to click the Active Records card and see:

* Patient number
* Patient name
* Location
* Assessment type
* Prosthetic / orthotic type
* Last activity date
* Current stage
* Record status

### 5.2.3 Active Patients

Optional separate card.

If required, the system can show **Active Patients** separately.

Meaning:

* Unique patients who currently have at least one active record.

This is different from Active Records.

Example:

* One patient has two active records.
* Active Patients count = 1
* Active Records count = 2

### 5.2.4 Today’s Activities

Instead of using “Today’s active records,” the better dashboard label is:

**Today’s Activities**

This can show today’s scheduled or recorded items, such as:

* Assessments
* Fittings
* Deliveries

Follow-ups should not appear as pending items because follow-ups are report-only according to the confirmed requirement.

---

## 5.3 Appointments / Date-Based Actions

Dashboard should include an Appointments or Date-Based Actions button/tab.

It should allow users to view or create:

* Assessment appointment
* Fitting appointment
* Delivery appointment

Delivery must be available in appointment creation and delivery records.

However, delivery must not be shown as a pending appointment.

Follow-ups should be recorded and reported, but should not appear as pending dashboard items.

---

## 5.4 Quick Actions

Dashboard must include Quick Actions.

Quick action buttons:

1. Register New Patient
2. Create New Record / Assessment
3. Create New Appointment
4. Add Fitting
5. Add Delivery
6. Add Follow-up

### 5.4.1 Register New Patient

User must be able to register:

* Local patient
* Foreign patient

### 5.4.2 Create New Record / Assessment

User must be able to create a new prosthetic or orthotic assessment under an existing patient number.

### 5.4.3 Create New Appointment

Appointment creation should support:

* Assessment
* Fitting
* Delivery

Follow-up should be handled in follow-up records and reports, not as a pending appointment queue.

---

## 5.5 Recent Activities

Dashboard must show recent activities.

Examples:

* New patient registered
* Assessment created
* Prescription selected
* Fitting date added
* Delivery date changed
* Follow-up added
* Document uploaded

Each activity should show:

* Date/time
* Patient number
* Patient name
* Activity type
* User
* Location

---

## 5.6 Top Navigation

Top navigation should include:

* Dashboard
* Patient Folder
* Records
* Reports

