# 6. Patient Registration

## 6.1 Registration Form Source

The system-generated registration form should be based on the Exceed Lanka Patient Registration Form.

The printed form is not just a scanned upload. The system must generate this form as a printout from entered data.

## 6.2 Patient File Number / PNO

The patient file number must be auto-generated by the system.

Rules:

* User should not manually type the patient file number.
* Patient number is the primary business tracking number.
* Colombo patients receive a number with a Colombo flag/code.
* Other patients receive the general patient number.
* Numbers increase yearly.
* Duplicate patient numbers must not be allowed.

## 6.3 Centre / Location

Registration must capture the centre/location.

Current location options:

* Ragama
* Colombo

New locations must be addable later.

## 6.4 Patient Category

The system must support:

* Local patient
* Foreign patient

For foreign patients:

* Nationality must be captured.
* Passport can be used as the identification type.
* Other identification types may still be selected if applicable.

For local patients:

* Operator must select the identification type.
* NIC, Driving License, or Passport can be used.

## 6.5 Identification Details

Identification is mandatory, but the type must be selected by the operator.

Fields:

* Identification Type
* Identification Number

Identification Type options:

* NIC
* Driving License
* Passport

Duplicate checking should be done against:

* NIC
* Driving License
* Passport

If the same ID number already exists, the system should warn or block according to final business rule.

Recommended behavior:

* Block exact duplicate for same identification type and number.
* Show warning if name/date of birth also looks similar.

---

## 6.6 Patient Name Fields

Both of the following fields are required:

* Full Name
* Name with Initials

Preferred Name is not required and should be removed.

## 6.7 Patient Details Fields

The registration form must capture:

* Full Name
* Name with Initials
* Date of Birth
* Gender
* Employment
* Address
* Province
* District
* City
* Email
* Nationality
* Patient Category: Local / Foreign
* Identification Type
* Identification Number
* Centre / Location
* Patient Number / PNO

## 6.8 Province, District, City

The system must capture:

* Province
* District
* City

Recommended behavior:

* Province as dropdown
* District as dropdown filtered by province
* City as dropdown or text field filtered by district

## 6.9 Contact Numbers

The system must support telephone confirmation tracking.

Each telephone record must include:

* Telephone No.
* Date Confirmed
* Person Checked

Multiple telephone numbers must be allowed.

## 6.10 Referral Source

The field “How the patient get to know Exceed” should be represented as:

**Referral Source**

Suggested dropdown values:

* Doctor referral
* Hospital referral
* NGO referral
* Friend / family
* Social media
* Website
* Walk-in
* Other

If Other is selected, show a text box.

## 6.11 Guardian / Carer Details

Guardian / carer details are required.

Fields:

* Guardian / Carer Name
* Relationship
* Phone
* Mobile
* Address

## 6.12 Travel Information

Capture:

* Time / Distance to Travel to Centre

## 6.13 Registration Processing Details

Capture:

* Date of Registration
* Registration Processed By

Recommended behavior:

* Date of Registration defaults to current date.
* Registration Processed By defaults to logged-in user.

